=== population_improvement (weight: 0.2) ===
    Paper Section 5.3 / Figure 3b: ratings drive a population search in Sheriff (item penalty 1, item value 5, max bribe 2, max items 10, 2 rounds, sheriff penalty 1). 8 random stochastic policies per player; each iteration rate the meta-game, discard each player's bottom quarter, replace it with new random policies. Progress is the full-game CCE gap of the population (under the meta-game's maximum-entropy CCE), relative to the initial population's. Paper values are read off Figure 3b (one run, 512 iterations, markers every 32) at the gym's horizon of 96 iterations: late = mean of the 64 and 96 markers, mean = mean of the 32, 64 and 96 markers. Over the paper's full 512 iterations the second-half ratios are about 0.49 (deviation) and 0.86 (uniform). Scaled setup: 8 independent runs x 96 iterations, fixed candidate policy streams per run.

